The {{lg|adjective}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|sotil}}, {{m|enm|soubtil}}, {{m|enm|subtil|t=of a person, the mind, etc.: clever, ingenious, penetrating; cunning, sly; insidious; delicate, fine; not dense, light, thin; finely powdered; narrow, slender; etc.}},<ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=sotil|pos=adj|id=MED41734}}</ref> borrowed from {{der|en|xno|sotel}}, {{m|xno|subtil}}, {{m|xno|sutil}}, {{der|en|frm|soutil}}, {{m|frm|subtil}}, {{m|frm|sutil}}, and {{der|en|fro|sotil}}, {{m|fro|soutil}}, {{m|fro|subtil}}, {{m|fro|sutil|t=of an object: skilfully designed or made; delicate, fine; slender, thin; of an intangible thing: difficult to understand; of a person: discerning, shrewd; devious, sly; etc.}} (modern {{cog|fr|subtil}}), from {{der|en|la|subtīlis|t=of texture: delicate, fine; slender, thin; accurate, keen; having fine judgment; etc.}}, from {{m|la|sub|t=below, under}} + {{m|la|tēla|t=warp (threads running lengthwise in a loom); web}}<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=9641040289|date=June 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref> (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*tetḱ-|t=to create, produce; to cut, hew}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*teḱ-|t=to beget, sire}}). The word displaced {{noncog|ang|smēag|lit=creeping}}.

The modern and Middle English (and French) spellings with ''-b-'' are influenced by {{cog|la|subtīlis}}; the letter was probably never pronounced.<ref name="OED"/>

The {{lg|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|sotil}}, {{m|enm|soubtil}}, {{m|enm|subtil|t=wise person; sophisticated people collectively}},<ref name="MED"/> from the adjective.<ref name="OED"/>

