===Etymology 2===
Partly from both of the following:<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9334871359|date=September 2024}}</ref>

* From {{inh|en|enm|sotilen}}, {{m|enm|subtile}}, {{m|enm|subtilien|t=to reflect on (something); to become mentally keen; to connive, scheme; to contrive, invent; to become pure or thin; to (cause something to) become light or thin; (''medicine'') to lighten or reduce (a diet)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sotilen|pos=v|id=MED41735}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|sotiller}}, {{m|xno|soutiller}}, {{m|xno|sutiller}}, {{der|en|frm|soutiller}}, {{m|frm|soutillier}}, and {{der|en|fro|soutillier|t=to make thin; to sharpen; to split hairs when arguing; to scheme, plot}}, from {{der|en|fro|sotil}}, {{m|fro|soutil}}, {{m|fro|subtil}}, {{m|fro|sutil|pos=n}} (see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]]) + {{m|fro|-ier|pos={{lg|suffix}} forming {{lg|infinitive}}s of first-{{lg|conjugation}} {{lg|verb}}s}}, partly influenced by {{der|en|la-lat|subtīliāre}}, the {{lg|present}} {{lg|active}} {{lg|infinitive}} of {{m|la-lat|subtīliō|t=to act craftily; to diminish}}, from {{der|en|la|subtīlis|pos=a}} (see etymology 1) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=suffix forming regular first-conjugation verbs}}.
* From {{m|en|subtle|pos=a}}.

