* {{homophones|en|step}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[grassland]]s of [[Eastern Europe]] and [[Asia]]. {{defdate|from 1671}}
#: {{cot|en|pampas|plain|prairie|savanna|veld|qq1=South America|qq2=North America|qq3=North America|qq4=North Africa|qq5=South Africa}}
#* {{RQ:Carlyle Sartor Resartus|chapter=Preliminary|page=3|passage=Nevertheless be it remarked, that even a Russian '''steppe''' has tumuli and gold ornaments {{…}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|author=w:William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|location=London|page=187|passage=Enkidu was the hairy man of the wild '''steppes''', and Gilgamesh was the hero of civilization; but now the contrast is between Gilgamesh, the king, the man of political power, the heroic man of action, the extrovert, and Utnapishtim, the man of religious authority, the introvert, the sage.}}
# A [[vast]], [[cold]], [[dry]], [[grassy]] [[plain]].
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2000|author=Mary Elizabeth v. N.|title=Steppe|work=Blue Planet Biomes|publisher=West Tisbury Elementary School|url=http://www.blueplanetbiomes.org/steppe.htm|passage=Grasslands: The '''Steppe''' biome is a dry, cold, grassland that is found in all of the continents except Australia and Antarctica. It is mostly found in the USA, Mongolia, Siberia, Tibet and China. There isn't much humidity in the air because '''Steppe''' is located away from the ocean and close to mountain barriers.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190411131857/http://www.blueplanetbiomes.org:80/steppe.htm|archivedate=11 April 2019}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Aaron Lake Smith|title=Peeling Oniontown|magazine={{w|Vice Magazine|VICE}}|url=https://www.vice.com/en/article/peeling-oniontown-0000126-v19n1/|date=2012-01-23|passage=After standing around on the dirt '''steppe''' for a bit, surveying the nearby pit-bull kennels and skeletal mountain tree line, I headed back to Dover to meet Renny Abrams, the town judge, at his bustling country store and gas station.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250502150417/https://www.vice.com/en/article/peeling-oniontown-0000126-v19n1/}}

====Usage notes====
* While the region may correspond to the steppe biome, it is uncommon to refer to the landscapes of Canada as steppes, in contrast to the more conventional usage of the term when describing the steppes of Asia or Russia.

