# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[flow]] in a continuous or steady manner, like a liquid.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=7|passage=beneath those banks where rivers now '''stream'''|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1934|passage=When I came to myself I was lying, not in the outer blackness of the Mohune vault, not on a floor of sand; but in a bed of sweet clean linen, and in a little whitewashed room, through the window of which the spring sunlight '''streamed'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To extend; to stretch out with a wavy motion; to float in the wind.
#: {{ux|en|A flag '''streams''' in the wind.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[discharge]] in a [[#Noun|stream]].
#: {{ux|en|The soldier's wound was '''streaming''' blood.}}
# {{lb|en|Internet}} To [[push]] [[continuous]] [[data]] (e.g. [[music]]) from a server to a client computer while it is being used (played) on the client.
# {{lb|en|Internet}} To [[livestream]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=w:F1NN5TER|title=Coming Out|date=1 March 2024|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3reFDwM0yIA|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240514163811/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3reFDwM0yIA|archivedate=14 May 2024|accessdate=15 May 2024|time=1:40|text=I ''did'' factor in the whole, like, "oh, I wonder if doing streaming, and the money that's kind of attached to it, is the reason I wanted to do this?", like, is it ''warping my brain?''  I did think about that.  I've '''streamed''' for years and it's been my entire life and I've made a lot of money off it, and I wondered if that's what's affecting me and making me want to do this.  And it's not.}}

