====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[topmost]] [[point#Noun|point]] or [[surface#Noun|surface]] of a [[thing]]; the [[apex]], the [[peak#Noun|peak]].
#: {{synonyms|en|acme|summity<q:obsolete>|zenith|Thesaurus:summit}}
## {{senseid|en|peak}} The [[high#Adjective|highest]] point of a [[hill#Noun|hill]], [[mountain]], or similar [[geographical]] [[feature#Noun|feature]].
##: {{ux|en|In summer, it is possible to hike to the '''summit''' of Mount Shasta.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|artist=w:Spiritbox|title=The Summit|album=[[w:Eternal Blue (album)|Eternal Blue]]|location=Portland, Or.|publisher=w:Rise Records|date=17 September 2021|oclc=1439270457|passage=How can I crawl up to reach those heights / And run? / The venom is what keeps me alive / The venom is what keeps me alive / Up to the '''summit''' at night / Desperate to find that beating heart of mine that always makes me run}}
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[vertex]] of a [[polygon]] or [[polyhedron]].
## {{lb|en|nautical|rail transport|road transport}} The highest point of a [[canal#Noun|canal]], [[railway]], [[road#Noun|road]], etc.
## {{lb|en|obsolete}}
### {{lb|en|botany}} {{synonym of|en|anther<t:the [[pollen]]-[[bearing]] part of the [[stamen]] of a flower>,stigma<q:rare><t:the sticky part of a flower that receives [[pollen]] during [[pollination]]>}}.
### {{lb|en|crystallography|rare}} One of the [[two]] vertices of a [[crystal#Noun|crystal]] with a [[rhombohedral]] [[shape#Noun|shape]] where the [[angle#Noun|angles]] of each [[face#Noun|face]] are [[equal#Adjective|equal]]; also, the highest point of a crystal with a [[pyramidal#Adjective|pyramidal]] or [[tetrahedral#Adjective|tetrahedral]] shape.
# {{lb|en|figurative}}
## The highest point of [[achievement]], [[development]], etc., that can be [[reach#Verb|reached]]; the [[acme]], the [[pinnacle#Noun|pinnacle]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1924 |author=Herbert Weir Smyth |title=Aeschylean Tragedy |chapter=VI. Orestea. I: Agamemnon |page=153 |text=Learning from others as from himself, he reached the '''summit''' of his development with his latest work.}}
## {{lb|en|politics}}
### {{lb|en|archaic}} The highest [[level#Noun|level]] of [[political#Adjective|political]] [[leadership]].
### {{senseid|en|gathering}}{{lb|en|by extension}} An [[assembly]] or [[gathering#Noun|gathering]] of the [[leader]]s of [[country|countries]] to [[discuss]] [[issue#Noun|issues]] of [[international#Adjective|international]] [[significance]]; also {{lb|en|loosely}}, an [[important]] or [[high-level]] gathering or [[meeting#Noun|meeting]].
###: {{ux|en|They met for an international '''summit''' on environmental issues.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Colloquially, {{senseno|en|peak}} is used for only the highest point of a mountain, whereas in mountaineering any point that is higher than surrounding points is a ''summit'', such as the South Summit of [[Mount Everest]]. These are distinguished by {{w|topographic prominence}} as {{m|en|subsummit|subsummits}} (low prominence) or ''independent summits'' (high prominence).

